From 78e70caf999b7471c5b671041f35760729dc5999 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 13:02:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 049/115] drm/panel: sw43402: set prepare_prev_first

prepare() sends the whole DCS init sequence, so it needs the DSI host
powered on first. Under the panel-bridge ordering the panel's pre_enable
runs before the host's unless the panel declares prepare_prev_first;
without it every init write fails with -EINVAL and the panel never comes
up. The tree this driver was written against ordered the calls from the
DSI manager itself, which is why it never needed the flag before.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43402.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43402.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43402.c
index 66551d919785..34e0f1f4b6a5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43402.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43402.c
@@ -488,6 +488,13 @@ static int lg_sw43402_probe(struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi)
 	 */
 	dsi->dsc = dsc;
 
+	/*
+	 * prepare() sends DCS, so the DSI host must power on first; without
+	 * this the panel-bridge runs prepare before the host and every write
+	 * fails -EINVAL.
+	 */
+	ctx->panel.prepare_prev_first = true;
+
 	drm_panel_add(&ctx->panel);
 
 	return mipi_dsi_attach(dsi);
